      "message": "@pbdr@google.com I believe we discussed this case, could you please chime-in and verify this change?\n\nIf I remember correctly, `ENABLE_ON_CONNECT` is a development feature intended to be used for testing-only, to simplify some of the automated workflows.\n\nIn production, bypassing user consent dialog (without prior explicit configuration/confirmation) is a user privacy violation.\n\n`LogicalDisplayMapper.isEnabledInLayoutLocked(logicalDisplay)` does not violate user\u0027s privacy because it is checking precise address of the external display, meaning the vendor is pre-configuring the system to work with a specific display(s).",
